WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:03.070
Oh boy, here we go again.

00:00:03.070 --> 00:00:04.190
SCP-001.

00:00:04.190 --> 00:00:10.800
Over 30 different bizarre anomalies claim
this number one spot in the database - and

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:13.110
in a sense, they’re all right.

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:14.260
Or are they?

00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:18.960
If you’re feeling confused already, that’s
fine, we don’t expect that to change.

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:23.409
Because today, we’re dealing with one of
the most strange and intricate 001 entries

00:00:23.409 --> 00:00:25.820
out there: Keter Duty.

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:28.069
Just pray you never get assigned to it.

00:00:28.069 --> 00:00:32.899
You see, when you work around weirdness, you
sometimes get a little weird yourself.

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:37.890
And nobody deals with more weirdness than
employees of the SCP Foundation.

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:43.519
They regularly rub elbows with everything
from godlike cicadas to hyper-infectious supernatural

00:00:43.519 --> 00:00:44.789
viruses.

00:00:44.789 --> 00:00:50.390
And as the famous Tom Jones song goes, “it’s
not unusual to suddenly take on anomalous

00:00:50.390 --> 00:00:53.969
traits after consistently working with anomalies
for years.”

00:00:53.969 --> 00:00:56.800
That’s how the lyrics go, right?

00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:01.890
Anyway, one of the Foundation’s most iconic
researchers, Dr. Jack Bright, is technically

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:04.620
just an anomalous necklace himself.

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:09.660
But outside of some famous exceptions, the
SCP Foundation is in the business of containing

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:15.230
anomalous entities, not hiring them on and
giving them a paycheck and retirement plan.

00:01:15.230 --> 00:01:20.340
That’s why, if you suddenly start displaying
anomalous traits while on the Foundation payroll,

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:24.720
you might receive a company memo assigning
you to the dreaded “Keter Duty.”

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:30.030
But what is Keter Duty, and what kind of anomalous
traits can get you assigned to it?

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:32.590
Let’s start with the second question first.

00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:37.380
The Official Keter Duty guidelines list a
surprisingly vast number of afflictions.

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:41.930
These include chronic anomalous illnesses,
such as Lycanthropy - turning into a werewolf

00:01:41.930 --> 00:01:47.310
- something called Stevenson Syndrome, and
the incredibly unpleasant-sounding Photonic

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:49.590
Gastric Discharge Syndrome.

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:53.230
You could also be placed on Keter Duty because
you’re suffering from the manifestation

00:01:53.230 --> 00:01:58.250
of spectral phenomena, including being haunted
by spirits, whether they’re there to torment

00:01:58.250 --> 00:01:59.890
you or protect you.

00:01:59.890 --> 00:02:05.280
The sudden expression of anomalous traits
in your DNA, which is unsettlingly vague will

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:11.280
also land you on Keter Duty, as will the awakening
of powerful magical or psionic abilities,

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:15.580
especially ones which could be used in a potentially
offensive manner.

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:20.230
The “Keter Duty” assignment - which involves
being relocated and forced to work in a different,

00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:25.910
highly secretive location that will be discussed
soon - is framed as a punishment for the people

00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:26.910
involved.

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:31.450
That way, it discourages Foundation employees
from ever trying to develop anomalous powers

00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:32.720
on purpose.

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:36.230
So what exactly is Keter Duty, and where does
it happen?

00:02:36.230 --> 00:02:40.170
To reinforce that “punishment” element
mentioned, the Foundation has spread lies

00:02:40.170 --> 00:02:45.310
among their own personnel about where the
job takes place, often involving being posted

00:02:45.310 --> 00:02:49.150
in some of the least desirable Foundation
areas imaginable.

00:02:49.150 --> 00:02:53.740
These include Point Nemo - the area of the
ocean farthest from any piece of land on earth

00:02:53.740 --> 00:03:00.440
- Pyongyang in North Korea, Stonehenge, Roswell,
Lunar Area-32, and a number of Foundation

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:02.130
waste disposal sites.

00:03:02.130 --> 00:03:08.319
However, the reality of where those on Keter
Duty end up is even stranger: Site-100, which

00:03:08.319 --> 00:03:13.190
in this particular instance, is the true SCP-001.

00:03:13.190 --> 00:03:17.800
This Thaumiel-class anomaly is perhaps the
most unique of all multi-anomaly Foundation

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:24.440
containment sites, a bizarre labyrinth of
non-euclidean geometry that defies true explanation.

00:03:24.440 --> 00:03:26.320
But we’ll do the best we can.

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:29.750
In a sense, Site-100 is a facility with a
mind of its own.

00:03:29.750 --> 00:03:34.870
It’s a sprawling underground base with a
layout that defies spacetime, and what’s

00:03:34.870 --> 00:03:38.520
more, it undergoes so-called “Migration
Events.”

00:03:38.520 --> 00:03:44.130
Every so often, it will begin to exhibit a
sense of dimensional instability, before teleporting

00:03:44.130 --> 00:03:47.040
to a different location somewhere on earth.

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:52.069
Currently, the primary entrance to Site-100
- known as Alpha Entrance - is located in

00:03:52.069 --> 00:03:56.530
the Southwest United States, though all signs
point to another migration event happening

00:03:56.530 --> 00:03:58.280
this very year.

00:03:58.280 --> 00:04:02.440
But knowing where the entrance is will only
get you so far.

00:04:02.440 --> 00:04:06.340
People assigned to Keter Duty are sent from
the Alpha Entrance to the Administration Sector

00:04:06.340 --> 00:04:11.130
to be given their initial breaching, at which
point, the true madness begins.

00:04:11.130 --> 00:04:13.489
Let’s take a look at a map of Site-100.

00:04:13.489 --> 00:04:15.560
Yikes.

00:04:15.560 --> 00:04:20.720
So there are ten major sectors in Site-100
that you should be aware of: Entrance Alpha,

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:28.330
Administration, Archives, Technological Containment,
Bio-Containment, Sapient Containment, Cognitohazardous/Memetic/and

00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:35.199
Semantic - or CMS Containment, Esoteric Containment,
Conceptual Containment, and the Core Sector.

00:04:35.199 --> 00:04:38.210
As you can tell, they have almost everything
covered here.

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:43.680
But just as insane as the anomalies that Site-100
contains and the methods they use to contain

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:46.979
them, is how you actually get around the site.

00:04:46.979 --> 00:04:50.380
Site-100 is a spatial anomaly of truly epic
proportions.

00:04:50.380 --> 00:04:55.490
While the Foundation is aware of the existence
of its component sectors, it’s impossible

00:04:55.490 --> 00:04:58.400
to map out any meaningful connections between
them.

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:02.909
It would be pretty much impossible to even
travel from one to another without passageways

00:05:02.909 --> 00:05:04.759
known as The Roots.

00:05:04.759 --> 00:05:08.490
However, these aren’t just mere portals
that you can hop through like the Ways in

00:05:08.490 --> 00:05:10.870
and out of the Wanderer’s Library.

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:16.349
Each Root between the sectors is its own complex
environment, with its own sets of protocols

00:05:16.349 --> 00:05:19.879
and rituals required to safely travel through
it.

00:05:19.879 --> 00:05:24.629
Root Aleph, the bridge between the Archives
and the inaccessible core of Site-100, is

00:05:24.629 --> 00:05:29.939
a Volcanic Beach blocked off by an apparently
limitless obsidian wall, where fish made from

00:05:29.939 --> 00:05:33.039
living rock swim in the nearby waters.

00:05:33.039 --> 00:05:37.460
Root Beth, connecting the core and Sapient
Containment, is a huge and sprawling funhouse

00:05:37.460 --> 00:05:39.210
hall of mirrors.

00:05:39.210 --> 00:05:43.449
Anyone who attempts to travel through it inevitably
ends up turned around and arrives back at

00:05:43.449 --> 00:05:46.229
their starting point in Sapient Containment.

00:05:46.229 --> 00:05:51.060
Root Daleth, the bridge that connects Conceptual
Containment and the Core, is a massive ocean

00:05:51.060 --> 00:05:54.779
that has resisted all attempts by the Foundation
to traverse it.

00:05:54.779 --> 00:06:00.449
Root Vav, the bridge between Esoteric Containment
and Conceptual Containment, is a massive field

00:06:00.449 --> 00:06:03.139
filled with unidentified fruit trees.

00:06:03.139 --> 00:06:07.610
Foundation expeditions have found that it
too seems impossible to traverse.

00:06:07.610 --> 00:06:11.910
One expedition team was trapped inside for
a whole year, until one member of the team

00:06:11.910 --> 00:06:14.469
expressed a desire to go home.

00:06:14.469 --> 00:06:18.400
At that point, they were immediately teleported
back to the starting point.

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:21.349
Root Tzaddi
connecting Administration to the CMS Sector,

00:06:21.349 --> 00:06:24.939
is a huge, lush forest on top of a floating
mountain.

00:06:24.939 --> 00:06:29.319
The only animals that seem to populate this
forest are non-anomalous flamingos.

00:06:29.319 --> 00:06:34.369
Next, we have Root Peh, the bridge between
the Archive and Administration, which appears

00:06:34.369 --> 00:06:38.680
to be a hallway on the fifth floor of a tenement
building in a city that the Foundation haven’t

00:06:38.680 --> 00:06:40.279
been able to locate.

00:06:40.279 --> 00:06:44.779
This building is populated by non-hostile
humanoid creatures, who will approach Foundation

00:06:44.779 --> 00:06:49.020
staff traversing Root Peh and invite them
into their apartments, offering to partake

00:06:49.020 --> 00:06:54.490
in recreational activities with them such
as video games, board games, or watching movies.

00:06:54.490 --> 00:06:58.699
The Foundation discourages its staff from
accepting any of these offers while on the

00:06:58.699 --> 00:06:59.699
job.

00:06:59.699 --> 00:07:05.240
And then there’s Root Shin, which connects
the Sapient and Conceptual containment sectors.

00:07:05.240 --> 00:07:10.419
This Root is unique in the sense that it acts
as a power generator for the rest of Site-100,

00:07:10.419 --> 00:07:15.800
as it’s filled with hundreds of large perpetual
motion machines producing a constant 8.7 gigawatts

00:07:15.800 --> 00:07:17.339
of electricity.

00:07:17.339 --> 00:07:21.680
These are only some of the many Roots illustrated
on the Site-100 diagram.

00:07:21.680 --> 00:07:25.589
As you’ve probably gathered by now, it’s
less like a conventional building and more

00:07:25.589 --> 00:07:29.050
like a whole crazy dimension unto itself.

00:07:29.050 --> 00:07:32.300
Why does the Foundation work to maintain such
a crazy place?

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:36.240
Wouldn’t it just be easier to keep it a
secret, and contain it like any other anomaly?

00:07:36.240 --> 00:07:42.520
Well Site-100 wouldn’t be given the SCP-001
designation if it wasn’t incredibly important.

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:48.259
If Site-100 was ever compromised, it would
lead to an inevitable K-Class End of the World

00:07:48.259 --> 00:07:53.919
Scenario, because the site is intrinsically
tied to the nature and containment of literally

00:07:53.919 --> 00:07:59.330
every single Keter-Class SCP in our universe
- hence the nickname “Keter Duty” for

00:07:59.330 --> 00:08:01.120
those working at the site.

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:06.029
In fact, an anomaly can’t even be classed
as a Keter if it isn’t given “permission”

00:08:06.029 --> 00:08:07.550
by Site-100.

00:08:07.550 --> 00:08:12.569
The various sectors of Site-100 cover the
entire spectrum of anomalies, and each sector

00:08:12.569 --> 00:08:17.330
is a massive panoptic structure connected
by networks of glass elevators.

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:22.129
Whenever a new Keter-Class SCP is discovered,
its name and a brief description of its anomalous

00:08:22.129 --> 00:08:26.610
traits will inscribe itself on one of the
walls in its corresponding sector.

00:08:26.610 --> 00:08:30.860
Ever been frustrated when the 05 Council refused
to sign off on an upgrade to Keter Class for

00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:34.880
a clearly dangerous SCP that poses extreme
risk of containment breach?

00:08:34.880 --> 00:08:40.089
Don’t blame them - it’s simply that Site-100
didn’t sanction the change.

00:08:40.089 --> 00:08:46.290
Any time that Site-100 sanctions a new SCP,
it also undergoes another unique process:

00:08:46.290 --> 00:08:52.519
It selects an SCP-001-K instance for the new
Keter, and creates a connection between them

00:08:52.519 --> 00:08:54.830
- using access points known as “Thresholds.”

00:08:54.830 --> 00:09:01.180
Think of it as simply opening a spatially-anomalous
door between two SCPs.

00:09:01.180 --> 00:09:08.029
Much like A Good Boy, another SCP vying for
the 001 slot, Site-100 has an intuitive grasp

00:09:08.029 --> 00:09:14.800
of the unseen connections between Keter-Class
anomalies, and each SCP-001-K instance is

00:09:14.800 --> 00:09:19.750
a complementary Keter Class that will essentially
cancel out the threat of its other half.

00:09:19.750 --> 00:09:25.589
Site-100 is a containment matchmaker, its
innate ability to use the anomalous to contain

00:09:25.589 --> 00:09:28.160
the anomalous is second to none.

00:09:28.160 --> 00:09:33.980
First, it took SCP-3984, an anomalous phenomenon
that seemed to prevent death from happening

00:09:33.980 --> 00:09:35.480
to all lifeforms.

00:09:35.480 --> 00:09:41.200
In order to mitigate the effects of 3984,
Site-100 opened a threshold between it and

00:09:41.200 --> 00:09:47.810
SCP-2935, also known as “O, Death” - an
alternate universe hidden beyond a limestone

00:09:47.810 --> 00:09:53.959
cavern where all life simultaneously ceased
to exist, even down to the bacterial level.

00:09:53.959 --> 00:09:58.829
By opening the threshold and allowing these
two absolute opposites to mix, it seemed to

00:09:58.829 --> 00:10:04.389
undermine the effects of both and create a
non-anomalous happy medium: Life, but mortal

00:10:04.389 --> 00:10:05.569
life.

00:10:05.569 --> 00:10:07.910
Next, SCP-5007.

00:10:07.910 --> 00:10:12.720
This terrifying underwater anomaly manifests
as a series of tentacle-like protrusions that

00:10:12.720 --> 00:10:18.829
snatch unfortunate creatures that get too
close, and assimilate them into its own mass.

00:10:18.829 --> 00:10:25.620
Site-100 cleverly opened a threshold to SCP-169,
a massive underwater arthropod known as The

00:10:25.620 --> 00:10:26.910
Leviathan.

00:10:26.910 --> 00:10:33.759
SCP-169 was tangled up by the tentacles, but
it’s too big to be fully consumed or assimilated,

00:10:33.759 --> 00:10:40.120
and the result is that 5007 is trapped in
a perpetually incapaciated state akin to choking,

00:10:40.120 --> 00:10:44.110
keeping it contained and stopping it from
going after anyone else.

00:10:44.110 --> 00:10:48.980
Let’s take a look at two even more hostile
and dangerous Keter-Class anomalies matched

00:10:48.980 --> 00:10:49.980
up by Site-100.

00:10:49.980 --> 00:10:58.250
First, we’ve got SCP-5501, an old camera
from the 1800s that comes with 18 photographs.

00:10:58.250 --> 00:11:02.800
These photographs act as a kind of portal
to an incredibly frightening alternate reality

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:08.279
that creatures regularly crawl out of, attacking
and killing anyone within reach.

00:11:08.279 --> 00:11:14.670
Site-100 found a perfect match for this nasty
customer: SCP-1983.

00:11:14.670 --> 00:11:18.959
This is a small house that acts as a portal
to a race of tall monsters with needle-like

00:11:18.959 --> 00:11:22.639
appendages that leave the house in search
of victims.

00:11:22.639 --> 00:11:27.779
When they catch these victims, they take out
their hearts, and bring them back to the nest.

00:11:27.779 --> 00:11:34.899
Site-100 opened a threshold into the SCP-1983
house and placed the 5501 photographs inside.

00:11:34.899 --> 00:11:39.540
As a result, the hostile creatures from both
dimensions now regulate each other’s populations

00:11:39.540 --> 00:11:41.240
by killing each other.

00:11:41.240 --> 00:11:43.879
Another job well done for Site-100.

00:11:43.879 --> 00:11:49.470
Another Keter-Class dealt with by Site-100
is SCP-PL-122.

00:11:49.470 --> 00:11:55.120
This is a deadly plot of land in Poland, which
decays and corrodes all matter - organic or

00:11:55.120 --> 00:11:58.210
inorganic - placed within its confines.

00:11:58.210 --> 00:12:02.050
This would be bad enough, but as you’ll
often find with anomalous plots of deadly

00:12:02.050 --> 00:12:05.139
land, its area of influence is growing.

00:12:05.139 --> 00:12:08.410
Even knowing about it can cause it to become
more powerful.

00:12:08.410 --> 00:12:14.740
But Site-100 found its perfect Keter-Class
counterpart: SCP-1262.

00:12:14.740 --> 00:12:19.550
This is a massive mass of plant matter that
grows at a truly astonishing rate, expanding

00:12:19.550 --> 00:12:22.399
by around seven kilometers an hour.

00:12:22.399 --> 00:12:29.560
Much like absolute death and absolute life,
by putting 1262 into SCP-PL-122, a healthy

00:12:29.560 --> 00:12:32.110
medium was found somewhere in between.

00:12:32.110 --> 00:12:38.629
And finally, perhaps the strangest and most
creative match Site-100 has ever pulled off:

00:12:38.629 --> 00:12:41.910
SCP-3852 and SCP-2547.

00:12:41.910 --> 00:12:49.139
3852 is an anonymous corpse that manifests
in small towns, sowing fear and suspicion.

00:12:49.139 --> 00:12:53.800
Eventually, a local person is believed to
be responsible for this murder, and is lynched

00:12:53.800 --> 00:12:57.990
in a rage by the townspeople as a form of
vigilante justice.

00:12:57.990 --> 00:13:00.920
The corpse then moves on to the next town.

00:13:00.920 --> 00:13:06.800
2547, if you can believe it, is even weirder:
It’s a pack of dogs led by an intelligent

00:13:06.800 --> 00:13:09.910
talking Coyote dressed as a priest.

00:13:09.910 --> 00:13:15.250
Site-100 had the truly galaxy-brain idea to
open a threshold and connect the two.

00:13:15.250 --> 00:13:20.190
As a result, whenever the corpse manifests
in the town, the dogs rampage in and take

00:13:20.190 --> 00:13:21.190
over.

00:13:21.190 --> 00:13:26.100
At that point, they set up a kind of ridiculous
kangaroo court, where a jury made up of people

00:13:26.100 --> 00:13:30.450
from the town are forced to find 3852’s
scapegoat innocent.

00:13:30.450 --> 00:13:36.170
If they don’t, the dogs will simply hold
the town’s water supply hostage until 3852’s

00:13:36.170 --> 00:13:37.829
anomalous effects pass.

00:13:37.829 --> 00:13:39.600
Such an obvious idea!

00:13:39.600 --> 00:13:41.770
Now why didn’t the Foundation think of that?

00:13:41.770 --> 00:13:47.060
Keter Duty may not be the most conventional,
easy, or attractive work, but like everything

00:13:47.060 --> 00:13:52.329
the Foundation does, making sure Site-100
can keep doing its job is a necessary part

00:13:52.329 --> 00:13:55.700
of keeping our world safe from anomalous threats.

00:13:55.700 --> 00:13:58.509
Now if you’ll excuse us, we need to get
going.

00:13:58.509 --> 00:13:59.509
Hmmm.

00:13:59.509 --> 00:14:01.499
Do you know which is the right Root out of
here?

00:14:01.499 --> 00:14:06.160
Now go check out “SCP-001 - Which is the
Real 001?”

00:14:06.160 --> 00:14:08.790
and “SCP-001 - When Day Breaks”

00:14:08.790 --> 00:14:12.600
for more on the mysterious SCP-001!

